WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
This is Safety and Training. We cover health and safety protocols, security operations, and staff training frameworks.

c2
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:20.000
Health, Safety and Security is a distinct department covering visitor safety, staff safety, fire protocols, food safety in the kitchen, and emergency evacuation drills.

c3
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:32.000
Security operations include crowd management during festivals, CCTV monitoring, valuables handling in the treasury, and coordination with local police for major events.

c4
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:44.000
Training and Development is a cross-cutting function that runs induction for new staff, role-specific training, and periodic refreshers on compliance and safety.

c5
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:56.000
Every department is required to complete an annual safety compliance training. Attendance is tracked and reported to the trust board.

c6
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:08.000
Food safety training is mandatory for anyone working in the kitchen, whether paid staff or volunteer. Certification is renewed every two years.

c7
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:20.000
Emergency response protocols include fire evacuation, first aid, medical emergencies during darshan, and coordination with hospitals for major incidents.

c8
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:32.000
Training records are maintained per person. Managers must sign off on role competency before assigning staff to safety-critical duties.
